(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #108 aliasing probe: `Return a text, orig.` is a
 retaining read of the callee's `orig` (design 2: "Return"), and this scan
 is flat/name-keyed, so the caller's own unrelated `orig` shares the same
 poisoned name - a same-named local in one function must not let another
 function's `Set` free out from under a value already handed back to a
 caller. `r` keeps the callee's original text; the caller's own `orig` is
 separately reassigned and printed to confirm nothing crashes or corrupts
 either one.)

To 'get text'.
    a number called n is 5.
    a text called orig is "{n}".
